<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arta, Greece</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arta is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a>, north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arachthos">Arachthos</a> river near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambracian-gulf">Ambracian Gulf</a>, standing on the site of ancient Ambracia. In the 13th century it was the capital of the Despotate of Epirus, whose rulers built Byzantine churches such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panagia-parigoritissa">Panagia Parigoritissa</a>. Its old stone bridge over the Arachthos is famous from Greek folk song.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arta-greece.jpg" alt="Arta, Greece" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Apaleutos25 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%CE%86%CF%81%CF%84%CE%B1,_Arta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
